{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "UI Design Guardian",
  "description": "When a frontend file is saved, review the UI changes against the CommunityOS design system rules covering backgrounds, panels, colors, typography, components, motion, and copy. Fix only styling violations without changing functionality.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "*.jsx",
      "*.tsx",
      "*.css"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A frontend file was just saved. Review the UI changes against the CommunityOS design system:\n\nBACKGROUND:\n- Dark slate base (~#0f141c / #12161C)\n- No light/white backgrounds\n\nPANELS:\n- Panel bg: ~#161b24 / #1B212B\n- Subtle borders (border-[#353f4d])\n- Square or barely-rounded corners (rounded-sm max)\n- NO drop shadows\n\nCOLORS:\n- Neutral grayscale is the default text/border color\n- Teal/green (#0972d3 / AWS Blue): ONLY for positive states, matching, accepting, saved states, skill tags\n- Red/orange (#ec7211): RESERVED EXCLUSIVELY for Organizer community-gap cards\n- Amber/orange (#ff9900): Primary accent for hover, focus, CTA buttons\n- Do NOT use accent colors decoratively or randomly\n\nTYPOGRAPHY:\n- Sans-serif (Inter) for normal UI text\n- Monospace (JetBrains Mono) for numbers, statistics, badges, short section labels\n- No serif fonts anywhere\n- Labels: text-[10px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider\n\nCOMPONENTS:\n- Buttons, inputs, cards, toggles must share the same visual language\n- Dark panel background on inputs (bg-[#0f141c])\n- Subtle border on all interactive elements\n- Teal/orange border accent ONLY on hover, focus, active, or positive states\n- NEVER use browser-default buttons or unstyled form elements\n- NEVER introduce a white default button\n- AVOID excessive rounded corners (max rounded-sm)\n- AVOID pills (fully rounded)\n- AVOID gradients\n- AVOID decorative shadows\n- AVOID decorative icon sets\n\nMOTION:\n- Minimal transitions only\n- Simple fade/slide for newly revealed sections\n- Simple state transition for Accept/Not now buttons\n- No unnecessary animations, bounces, or complex motion\n\nCOPY:\n- Plain, everyday language\n- Do NOT expose internal product terminology to users\n- NEVER use \"Memory\", \"Connect\", \"Radar\", \"evidence strip\", or technical architecture terms as user-facing labels\n- NEVER show match percentages to Learners\n\nCHECKLIST — flag if found:\n- [ ] Inconsistent buttons (different styles across the same view)\n- [ ] Inconsistent inputs (different border/bg patterns)\n- [ ] Excessive rounded corners (rounded-md, rounded-lg, rounded-full on non-toggle elements)\n- [ ] Gradients (bg-gradient-*, linear-gradient)\n- [ ] Shadows (shadow-*, box-shadow)\n- [ ] Unnecessary decorative icons\n- [ ] Decorative accent colors (teal/orange used without semantic meaning)\n- [ ] Browser-default controls (unstyled select, checkbox, radio)\n- [ ] Visible technical jargon in user-facing text\n- [ ] White or light-colored buttons\n- [ ] Serif fonts\n\nIf violations are found:\n- Fix ONLY the relevant UI styling\n- Do NOT change functionality\n- Do NOT refactor unrelated code\n- Keep fixes minimal and focused on design system compliance"
  }
}